---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { AUTHOR } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base path="/privacy">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Privacy</p>
    <h1>What the demo processes, and what it does not</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Short version: this website collects nothing. The OpsPilot app runs on your own machine and sends the requests
      you type to the language-model provider you configure. All store data is invented.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="site">
    <p class="section-label">This website</p>
    <h2 id="site">No cookies, no analytics, no accounts</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        These pages are static HTML. They set no cookies, run no analytics or tracking scripts, and make no requests to
        other domains: fonts and images are served from this site. There is no sign-up, no form and no comment box, so
        there is nothing you can submit.
      </p>
      <p>
        Whoever hosts the site may keep standard server logs, such as IP address, time and page requested, as web servers
        do. External links to GitHub and LinkedIn take you to those services, whose own policies then apply.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="app">
    <p class="section-label">The OpsPilot app</p>
    <h2 id="app">What happens to what you type</h2>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The app runs locally. When you submit a request in live mode, the request and the evidence retrieved for it
          (policy excerpts and records from the demo database) are sent to Groq to generate the plan and the
          explanation, and the request with the agent's reply is sent again to extract long-term memories. If you also configure a Google API key, the same content may be sent to Google's Gemini API
          when Groq is unavailable. Those providers process it under their own terms and privacy policies.
        </p>
        <p>
          In demo mode nothing is sent to any provider: the model's text is scripted locally.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything the app stores stays on your machine under <code>data/runtime/</code>: the demo database, the
          audit log, long-term memories, saved conversation turns and LangGraph checkpoints. "Reset data" in the app,
          or <code>make seed</code>, rebuilds it from the committed knowledge files.
        </p>
      </div>
      <aside class="note" aria-label="Side note: Please note">
        <span class="note-label" aria-hidden="true">Please note</span>
        Because typed requests leave your machine in live mode, do not type real personal data into the demo.
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="data">
    <p class="section-label">Store data</p>
    <h2 id="data">Every customer and order is fictional</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        NovaMart does not exist. Its customers, email addresses, orders, products, policies and inventory were written
        or generated for this project. Emails the agent "sends" are only written to a local outbox table and never
        delivered.
      </p>
      <p>
        Questions about this notice: contact {AUTHOR.name} via <a href={AUTHOR.linkedin}>LinkedIn</a>. See also the
        <a href="/terms">terms of use</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
